 34CL c  1982Va02: 32-35-MeV {+12}C beams from the Utrecht Van de Graaff        
 34CL2c  accelerator impinged on a target of 99.92%-enriched 380-|mg/cm{+2}     
 34CL3c  {+24}Mg on Au backing. |g rays were detected using a large solid angle 
 34CL4c  Compton-suppression spectrometer (LACSS) and a HPGe central detector in
 34CL5c  combination with four gating Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g,      
 34CL6c  |g|g-coin, and |g|g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |g-ray branching ratios,   
 34CL7c  and mixing ratios. Comparisons with shell-model calculations. Also     
 34CL8c  measured the {+31}P(|a,n|g){+34}Cl reaction for lifetimes using DSAM.  
